The compiled extension (csrc/gcharge.cpp) is built against Psi4's C++ headers
and resolves Psi4 symbols from Psi4's own core module at load time.  Psi4 is
LGPL-3.0-only; see https://github.com/psi4/psi4.


Third-party code
================

src/psi4_swig_pcm/charges.py adapts the diffuse-charge construction in Psi4's
driver/procrouting/proc.py (_set_external_potentials_to_wavefunction), Copyright
(c) 2007-2026 The Psi4 Developers, LGPL-3.0-only like this project.

The compiled extension (psi4_swig_pcm/_gcharge) contains code from the pybind11
headers, Copyright (c) 2016 Wenzel Jakob, under the BSD 3-Clause License
(LICENSES/pybind11-BSD-3-Clause.txt).  That applies to built packages only: the
source in this repository contains no pybind11 code.

packages/moist is a build recipe for moist (https://github.com/lukaswittmann/moist,
Copyright Lukas Wittmann, MPL-2.0).  It downloads moist's source when the package is
built and contains none of it, apart from the context lines of a one-line patch to
moist's copy of FINUFFT (Apache-2.0) in packages/moist/patches.

src/psi4_swig_pcm/moist_contractions.py is adapted from moist's own PySCF host
(python/moist/pyscf.py in moist 1.1.0-alpha.1, by Lukas Wittmann): the
contractions of moist's density response (PySCFHost._fock_lsf and
_gradient_lsf) and the nuclear potential at moist's Gaussian probes.  It remains
under the Mozilla Public License 2.0 (LICENSES/MPL-2.0.txt), moist's license;
its header says what was changed.

src/psi4_swig_pcm/moist_host.py (a prototype), the rest of the Psi4 host for
moist, is this project's own and LGPL-3.0-only.  It drives moist's coupling
protocol through moist's public Python interface, in the order moist prescribes
for a host.  moist itself is imported at run time, from the package
packages/moist builds.

src/psi4_swig_pcm/cavity.py is derived from PySCF (pyscf/solvent/pcm.py and
pyscf/solvent/grad/pcm.py, v2.11, https://github.com/pyscf/pyscf; Author:
Xiaojie Wu <wxj6000@gmail.com>; the gradient module was itself copied from
GPU4PySCF with modifications), Copyright 2014-2023 The PySCF Developers. All
Rights Reserved.  It remains under the Apache License, Version 2.0
(LICENSES/Apache-2.0.txt).  The modifications are described in that file's
header.  PySCF's NOTICE file follows, as Apache-2.0 section 4(d) requires.

